# Criterion 5 - branch protection applied and verified

Applied 2026-09-26T12:56:47Z by the orchestrating session, after #117 (a45857b) made
Quality gate report on every PR.

## 1. Protection is on, with the five contexts

$ gh api repos/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/branches/main/protection
{"allow_deletions":false,"allow_force_pushes":false,"approvals_required":0,"contexts":["Quality gate","Issue refs","Strip both-samples-removed + analyze + test","Strip feature-flags-removed + analyze + test","Strip tasks-removed + analyze + test"],"enforce_admins":true,"strict":false}

Docs check is deliberately NOT required: it still filters at the workflow
level, so it never reports on a code-only PR. Requiring it would recreate
the deadlock #117 removed, in the other direction.

## 2. A direct push to main is rejected

$ git commit --allow-empty && git push origin HEAD:main
remote: error: GH006: Protected branch update failed for refs/heads/main.
 ! [remote rejected]  HEAD -> main (protected branch hook declined)
(probe commit discarded afterwards; main unchanged)

## 3. A docs-only PR is Mergeable - the case that was impossible before #117

Throwaway PR #256, single file under docs/:
  Docs check                                     pass   33s
  Issue refs                                     pass   6s
  Quality gate                                   pass   6s
  Strip both-samples-removed + analyze + test    pass   6s
  Strip feature-flags-removed + analyze + test   pass   5s
  Strip tasks-removed + analyze + test           pass   5s

$ gh pr view 256 --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus
  MERGEABLE / CLEAN

Quality gate is green in seconds because #117 skips the expensive steps
inside the job when no changed path can affect them. It REPORTS, which is
what branch protection needs; it does not claim the code was tested.

---

## Addendum 2026-09-26: enforce_admins turned OFF at the owner's request

Section 2 above is no longer true of the live repository, and is kept as the
record of what was verified when protection was first applied.

The owner works solo, so requiring every change - including their own one-line
fixes - to go through a pull request cost more than it bought. `enforce_admins`
protects a branch from *other* people with write access; there are none here.

    $ gh api -X DELETE repos/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/branches/main/protection/enforce_admins

Verified by a real push rather than by reading the API back:

    $ git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: verify admin can push directly ..."
    $ git push origin HEAD:main
    To https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter.git
       07f23c82b92..19b4b474a93  HEAD -> main

That empty commit is left on `main` deliberately: it is the proof, it carries a
`Refs` trailer explaining itself, and removing it would need a force push,
which is still disabled.

### What is still enforced

    enforce_admins:     false   <- changed
    contexts:           Quality gate, Issue refs, and the three Strip variants
    approvals required: 0
    allow_force_pushes: false
    allow_deletions:    false

So the part that actually guards quality is intact: **a pull request whose
checks are red still cannot be merged**, by anyone. What changed is only that
the owner may push straight to `main` without opening a pull request first.

Criterion 5 of #58 remains satisfied - it asked that `main` be protected with
Quality gate required, and it is. `enforce_admins` was never named by the
criterion; it came from the payload drafted on the issue.
